  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Cabinet Vétérinaire of Dr Jackowski, at 256 avenue Maréchal Lyautey in Cavalaire-sur-Mer, treats dogs, cats and small exotic pets in the area. It is a sole-proprietorship veterinary business registered in Cavalaire-sur-Mer since 2014 according to the Sirene register, and the practice has a Facebook page where it posts its news.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to Golfe de Saint-Tropez Tourisme, the practice sees patients <strong>without an appointment</strong> Monday to Friday from 9am to 12pm and from 3pm to 7pm, and on Saturday from 9am to 12pm, all year round. To reach the practice, call 04 94 46 58 82. The list of the town's vets published by Cavalaire-sur-Mer town hall gives the same number.</p>
      <p>On appointments, the practice says "by appointment" on its Facebook page, which the page as displayed today does not allow us to confirm: the safest option is to call before you come, especially with a dog to be examined outside peak times.</p>
      <p>As for the address, the town hall says "avenue du Maréchal Lyautey" (256 in its 2024 and 2025 guides) and the Sirene register says "Le Goéland building, avenue Maréchal Lyautey", whereas the tourist office page writes "Promenade de la Mer": take avenue du Maréchal Lyautey.</p>
      <h2>Emergencies and out-of-hours care</h2>
      <p>The practice does not announce a 24/7 emergency service on the pages read. For a night or Sunday emergency, call the practice, then another vet in the area: the Cavalaire-sur-Mer town guides publish, for Dr Tison's clinic, the town's other vet (269 boulevard Pasteur, 04 94 64 08 52), a separate emergency number, which has changed between editions. Check it before you leave.</p>
      <div class="callout">Worth checking before you go: whether an appointment is required or not (two versions) and what to do at night.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>A <a href="/en/fiche-toiletteur-cavalaire">groomer</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-camping-cavalaire">Cavalaire campsite</a> are nearby if you are staying in the area with your dog. Dr Tison's clinic is the town's second one.</p>
